// Le Douzième Coup · chapter 8, the one who stays, second half (the abbey of Sainte-Aure, taken in 555, seat of
// the Veilleurs ; afternoon and night of 17 June 601). The gate, where one gives a name (`r:entre_nom` |
// `r:entre_medaille` | `r:entre_jeton`). Cloister hub: the church and the held note, the choir taken by its own vote,
// the twelfth stall (Tiphaine's letter: `r:sait_levier`, `r:sait_deux`), Tiphaine woken for the time of a pinch,
// the chapter house (the Book, if it was saved: `r:sait_levier`, `r:sait_double`, `r:sait_cuivre`), the annals (the
// line of 16 June 541, the last volume), the infirmary and its chalk, the water clock (`r:sait_hoquets`), the
// gardeners' door (Colin), the coffers of returns (`r:sabot_rendu`), the general Roll, and the Doyenne Ysoline
// (`r:veilleurs_amis`, `r:veilleurs_parvis`). Evening: the Regent Odeline on her way to the Oath
// (`r:regente_depeche`, `r:regente_doute`), her interview with the Master of Sands (`r:tour_blanche` |
// `r:tour_noire`, `r:aubespin_flaire`), Line behind a blind (`r:line_vue_abbaye`), the midnight walk (B08).
var P = {};
